-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Movie
  Publisher   Imagine, 1986
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        M.O.V.I.E. (1986)(Imagine)[a][a].z80
  MD5         facf9b90032759b7012abd91602b4b45

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu, its cheats and the Next
  start-up. The menu's Presentation line adds more; see the note. Game logic
  is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu, are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Painted 1930s noir colours: the hero, the other characters,
              furniture, walls and floors, and the icon panel with metal
              frames, ivory symbols and a wood-gripped pistol; the moving
              selector keeps its original yellow. Source: Enhanced colours:
              Jon Attree.

  Pace        original

  Changes     1.0: Optional Enhanced colours follow the original masked
              drawing on Layer 2: native clipping, shared edges and screen
              copies; the icon panel is painted once at start-up and only over
              the original set bits. Original game logic, delays and sound
              untouched. Full hidden 48K ROM; highest bank 47.

  Note        48K release with its beeper sound and the original loading
              screen. Default keeps the original monochrome look; no colour-
              clash-removal claim. Enhanced, off by default: painted 1930s
              noir colours for the figures, rooms and the icon panel; the
              moving selector keeps its original yellow. Disable DMA is a CPU-
              copy fallback. Fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: the female
              character's Enhanced sprite still needs work. In JNext, Enhanced
              is up to 1.75 percent slower than the original in sampled
              windows, within the 2 percent target. Missing: natural play to
              the end; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Enemies don't move
   3  Enemies don't shoot
   4  Skip final film check
   5  Start with film reel

  Archive Movie POK (MD5 7955ff07). Shooting and final-film entries translated
  to verified sites; the archive's broad return and film edits were unsafe.
  The film options are helpers, not instant completion.

